
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Subject: imperative mood, under 70 characters, no trailing period.
#          "add crawler labelling check", not "added" or "adds".
#
# type   feat     a new finding, check or capability
#        fix      corrects wrong behaviour or wrong documentation
#        docs     README, CONTRIBUTING, references/, SKILL.md prose
#        refactor no behaviour change
#        test     tests and fixtures
#        chore    housekeeping
#        ci       workflows and checks
#        deps     dependency changes
#        Append ! before the colon for a breaking change: feat!: ...
#
# scope  ddos-guardian  the skill as a whole, SKILL.md, frontmatter
#        scripts        waf-assess.py, waf-report.py, waf_finding_templates.py
#        references     the reference documents
#        readme         README.md
#        contributing   CONTRIBUTING.md and .github/
#        Omit the scope if the change genuinely spans everything.
#
# Body: wrap at 72 columns. Explain WHY this change is needed -- the diff
# already shows what changed. Name the invariant if the change touches one
# (standard library only / no network / never mutates AWS).
#
#
# Refs: #<issue>
#
# Enable this template with:  git config commit.template .gitmessage
